  "notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds; business-type funds on accrual basis (net position). Treated as cash basis; beginning/ending cash = total governmental fund balances (no liabilities; all assets are cash, CDs, county treasurer cash). Transfers net to zero in Total column (General +6,025, nonmajor -6,025); recorded gross. Balance sheet uses government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (mixes governmental modified cash and business-type accrual). Business-type reported receipts = total operating revenues 168,369 + interest 2,428 (no single printed total). General fund detail uses the Combining Statement of General Fund Departments Total column (10 department columns, more than 6, so Total used); the General Fund budgetary comparison (p10) is not recorded separately to avoid double counting. Function for mixed-department object lines set to general government with review. Zero-actual budget lines (transfers, capital projects expenditure) included with amount 0. Statement of cash flows (p8-9) not used (cash basis). Read pages 1-16 of 16."
